17
00:00:52,969 --> 00:00:55,929
correct solution regardless of the steps
it took to

18
00:00:55,929 --> 00:00:59,450
get there. Process based oversight, on the
other hand,

19
00:00:59,689 --> 00:01:03,929
currently relies on human understandable
task decompositions with direct

20
00:01:04,010 --> 00:01:08,569
supervision of intermediate steps. This
approach supervises the reasoning

21
00:01:08,569 --> 00:01:13,609
process itself, including all intermediate
steps. It ensures that

22
00:01:13,609 --> 00:01:16,290
each step leading to the final result is
logical

23
00:01:16,290 --> 00:01:19,849
and correct. For example, in solving a
math problem,

24
00:01:20,349 --> 00:01:23,030
every calculation and logical step taken
by the model

25
00:01:23,030 --> 00:01:26,670
would be evaluated for correctness. There
is figure 8.6

